Repository-wide rg mprotect / MAP_FIXED / SYS_MMAP / SYS_MUNMAP review:
Native dispatch: kernel/src/arch/x86_64/syscall.rs 50/51/52.
Native sys_mprotect calls process::mmap::sys_mprotect, not an emulation.
process/mmap.rs: sys_mprotect validates UserRange, normalized protection,
full ledger coverage, anonymous policy, present PTE ownership and complete
preflight_protect ledger plan before update_permissions_expected. It then
invalidates changed ranges through memory::tlb and commits the ledger.
map_anonymous_kind: checked_page_layout and UserRange precede preflight_replace
and map_fixed_transaction (which performs replacement).
sys_munmap: checked_page_layout and UserRange precede preflight_unmap,
journal staging and remove_expected_mapping.
No kernel VM implementation added or modified by this phase.
Existing target-gated mmap/munmap exports remain unchanged. The native static
archive retains them; no separate export registration mechanism is necessary.
MAP_NATIVE_THREAD remains absent from the public C header.
Hardware user-write fault/SMP stale-TLB injection: NOT_RUN by mman fixture;
its permission check uses independent kernel writable-PTE validation via
syscall 88 before and after restoring RW permissions.
